    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "This report is divided into six sections: 1) how and why firms acquired CAD/CAE, summarizing the responses given by firms to interview questions; 2) current uses of CAD/CAE, drawing on a literature review, user survey, and interviews; 3) characteristics of firms and markets that foster the use of CAD/CAE, also drawing on a literature review, user survey, and interviews; 4) benefits of CAD/CAE for AEC firms, describing how firms are using advanced computer technologies for strategic advantage; 5) a discussion some \"reasons behind the reasons\" firms acquire CAD/CAE; 6) recommendations for using CAD/CAE, with a forward view of what companies might do to sustain competitive advantage based on CAD/CAE, and an outline of some areas for further research.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
